---
import InformationPage from "../components/InformationPage.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import "../styles/information.css";
---
<SiteLayout title="How We Research Fundraising Providers | FundraisingDirectory.net" description="How our directory uses provider sources, verification dates, missing-data labels and placement disclosures.">
  <InformationPage eyebrow="Research standards" breadcrumbLabel="How we research" title="Read the evidence before choosing a provider." intro="The directory summarizes documented programs so you can investigate a shortlist. A listing or verification label is not an endorsement or a guarantee of results.">
    <section><h2>Sources and dates</h2><div><p>Provider profiles link to the sources used for their research, such as official program pages, pricing documentation and eligibility terms. Source check dates identify when the information was reviewed. “Sources checked” means the record has a verified research status; it does not mean every financial or operational detail is known.</p><p>“Last verified” is the recorded verification date, not a guarantee that terms remain unchanged. Individual claims can be researched at different times. Read the source dates and qualifications and confirm current terms directly with the provider. We do not promise a fixed review interval.</p></div></section>
    <section><h2>Missing information</h2><div><p>“Not yet researched” means our research is incomplete. “Not published by provider” means research did not establish a term. “Not applicable” means the field does not apply. None of these labels means a fee is zero. Research-in-progress labels are neutral and do not certify a provider.</p><p>Effort ratings are editorial assessments of the documented workflow, not measured volunteer hours or guaranteed ease. Finder recommendations use documented group, program and constraint fit; missing data limits confidence. Program profits, platform fees and payment processing fees are different economic models.</p></div></section>
    <section><h2>Featured and sponsored placements</h2><div><p>Featured means additional visibility, not endorsement. The homepage selection is fixed editorially, not a rotating advertisement. Eligibility requires active status, current source review, a verification date within 90 days, standard or anchor-quality research completeness, and researched economics, requirements, timing and logistics for every listed program. If the selected record fails those checks at build time, no replacement is chosen automatically.</p><p>Paid placements are labeled Sponsored. When an affiliate or other compensated relationship is recorded, affected profile links include a disclosure. Internal affiliate research does not influence Finder ranking or verification. The absence of an affiliate research result is not proof that no commercial program exists.</p></div></section>
    <section><h2>Corrections and submissions</h2><div><p>Provider submissions are requests for editorial review and do not publish automatically. To report a factual issue or supply an authoritative source, use <a href="/contact/">our contact email</a>. Planning guides show their recorded update dates; incomplete topic routes stay labeled and excluded from search indexing until ready.</p><p><a href="/providers/">Browse providers</a> or <a href="/ideas/">explore planning guides and ideas</a>.</p></div></section>
  </InformationPage>
</SiteLayout>
